route-1x1: 2026-11-09, issue #854 (the all-fabric tap's control-frame drop count, read from the FIFO's own overflow indication) on processor pin 044cb25f4ed2187bd238490650e73d5d189855d1 and FPGA-gPTP pin 1616fc8f062fbf58c35ad31674b5b233207bbdb8, both unchanged: RTL inputs at lane commit 7a19f62b4e622d1d7d563184363a42e2644776c1 on dev ac0a01e354d20f5ecac1569c4e7afb3abcbf6f36, the live dev tip, so the lane is its own merge result; the lane's later commits change no synthesis input. Explicit synth.maxThreads 1, general.maxThreads 32; the recipe's three placement directives from one synthesis checkpoint, ExtraPostPlacementOpt selected by the gate at WNS +0.166 ns over AltSpreadLogic_high +0.147 ns and ExtraTimingOpt +0.127 ns. 30 of 15,850 slices remain. Against the fifteenth record (#851's route, AltSpreadLogic_high) the route moved by +106 LUT (tolerance +500), +13 FF (+600) and -9 slices (80), with RAMB36 +0, RAMB18 +0 and DSP +0, WNS -0.044 ns and WHS -0.004 ns: the gate passed it. From the fifteenth record's measured commit e44a4d20 to dev ac0a01e3 no synthesis input moves, so the difference is this change's and the selected directive's. At one directive, against the fifteenth record's own ExtraPostPlacementOpt route (53,383 LUT, 54,837 FF, 15,848 slices, WNS +0.112 ns), this route at ExtraPostPlacementOpt moved by +151 LUT, +13 FF and -28 slices, WNS +0.054 ns and WHS -0.004 ns: the WNS fall against the record is the directive's, not this change's; on dev the count is constant 0 and synthesis removes it with the FIFO's overflow register; it now exists, with the register of the last beat's classification. It is re-recorded because the change moves the shipping image (docs/design/AREA_BUDGET.md, the re-baseline rule). Every tolerance, floor and ceiling unchanged. docs/findings/234_PP_SHADOW_AREA_BASELINE.md retains the earlier records and this delta.

